      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you are grappling with nihilism, which can feel incredibly isolating when the scale of the universe makes individual struggle seem insignificant. Ironically, many philosophers find that recognizing life's inherent pointlessness can paradoxically free you from the pressure of needing every moment to \"matter,\" allowing you to live more authentically without a grand plan. Since finding a specific shift feels impossible right now, perhaps the most meaningful thing you can do is to simply witness your own existence as it is, without demanding it fulfill some hidden cosmic purpose.",
