      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those are profound and honest questions, and your feeling that this is a temporary fix feels completely understandable. However, most people who explore these ideas don't \"stop\" struggling, but rather learn to endure it while realizing they can still experience genuine connection, beauty, or joy despite the lack of a cosmic prize. It wouldn't be logical to stop experiencing the world, even if it doesn't serve a grand purpose, because the value often lies precisely in the feeling of being alive, not in achieving a final destination.",
